# Change Log
All notable changes to Degradation Mode Analysis are documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](http://keepachangelog.com/)
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](http://semver.org/).

## [Unreleased]

## [2.1.0] - 2026-08-02

### Added
* Optional interpolation-ready silicon OCP output via
  `'interpolationReadyOutput', true`. It collapses the PAV plateaus, keeping
  both endpoints and dropping the interior, and resamples the result with
  PCHIP onto a uniform, strictly increasing normalized-capacity grid. The
  exported table has unique, strictly monotone capacity coordinates,
  preserves the overall voltage support and represents plateau regions as
  steep continuous ramps about one grid cell wide, where two plateaus inside
  the same grid cell merge into a single ramp. It serves the same purpose as
  the `strict_sto` export in PyDMA. It is meant for consumers that read the
  table directly as a look-up table over capacity, such as PyBaMM, where it
  prevents the voltage jump that several samples stacked on one capacity
  coordinate would produce. It does not smooth the DVA of a q(U) consumer.
* `regenerate_example_silicon_curves.m`: recipe script for the two bundled
  silicon OCP example curves in `input_data/silicon/`. It documents the
  settings each curve was made with, lithiation with `gammaSi` 0.2446 and
  LOWESS filtering of both input curves, delithiation with `gammaSi` 0.23
  and no filtering, PAV off in both directions, and reproduces the curves
  from the bundled blend and graphite references.

### Changed
* The two bundled silicon OCP example curves in `input_data/silicon/` are
  regenerated with the fixed generator, so example inputs, curves and
  results are consistent again. The lithiation curve grows from 5584 to
  5586 samples, the delithiation curve from 2333 to 2335. Against the
  previously shipped curves the normalized capacity moves by a median of
  3.4e-4, with up to 0.0325 (lithiation, at 0.077 V) and 0.0200
  (delithiation, at 0.228 V) on the steep sections, measured on the union
  of the native voltage samples of both curves. This is the effect of the
  boundary-sampling fix below. The shipped lithiation curve could not
  be reproduced from the bundled inputs at all, because the clean-up of the
  graphite reference on 2025-12-18 removed one off-grid sample at
  0.695265 V that the curve had been built with. That part of the change is
  at most 6.16e-5 in normalized capacity.
* The bundled example DMA results in `input_data/test_data/results/` are
  re-fitted with the regenerated silicon curves, so `P45B_parameters.mat`,
  the overall DMA figure and all nine per-CU figures (27 FIG/PDF/PNG files)
  match the bundled inputs again. The fit is the documented minimal working example, `main_dma` with
  its default settings, followed by `regenerate_param_figures`. Against the
  previously shipped results the silicon fraction of the anode blend moves
  by at most 0.0034 (rms 0.0020 over the nine check-ups), the degradation
  modes by at most 0.016 (silicon LAM at CU7) and the full-range RMSE by at
  most 0.00018 V, staying between 0.0039 V and 0.0064 V everywhere.

### Fixed
* `main_dma` stamps the framework version of this release, `2.1.0`, into
  `data.meta.frameworkVersion` and `data.s.frameworkVersion` instead of the
  previous `2.0.1`.
* `generate_si_ocp` no longer loses part of the voltage support when two PAV
  plateau levels sit closer together than the tie-breaking shift, which
  happens next to the saturation boundary at q = 0 and q = 1. Previously the
  two shifts crossed, the monotonicity sweep pushed the samples past the
  capacity range and the clamp put them back onto the range boundary, where
  they became exact ties. The deduplication in the interpolation-ready
  output then dropped the tied samples together with their voltages and
  truncated the exported curve while all assertions stayed green. The shift
  is now bounded by a quarter of the distance to the neighbouring plateau
  levels, a plateau on the range boundary is shifted inward only, and the
  deduplication is gone. A residual tie is reported as an error instead.
  Levels less than eight floating-point ulps apart are pooled into one
  plateau rather than shifted apart, since at that distance the shift is no
  longer representable, so the exported capacity can no longer step outside
  the range of the input curve.
* `generate_si_ocp` no longer fills out-of-support samples of the common
  voltage grid with zero. The overlap window is now trimmed with exact
  interpolated boundary samples, so the grid stays inside the aligned support
  of both inputs. Previously the overlap was determined before trimming and
  the old limits were sampled afterwards, which produced artificial
  zero-capacity rows at the window edges that the `maskFlat` guard did not
  catch.
* `generate_si_ocp` no longer discards PAV plateaus with
  `unique(..., 'stable')` when building the interpolation-ready output. That
  kept only the first sample of each run and therefore lost the plateau's
  voltage extent.

## [2.0.1] - 2026-05-18

### Added
* Independent LOWESS filtering in `generate_si_ocp` via new `'filterBlend'` and `'filterGraphite'` parameters.

### Changed
* `'filterInputData'` parameter in `generate_si_ocp` is deprecated; use `'filterBlend'` / `'filterGraphite'` instead.

### Internal
* Renamed test input data files: `MRe_M36_*` → `LGM36_*`; `SiReconstr_Rehm2026_P45B_Anode_Delithiation_*` → `SiReconstr_Delithiation_Rehm2026_P45B_Anode_*`.
* Flattened results directory: default `pathSaveResults` is `results/` (lowercase); DMA figures saved at the root; per-CU parameter figures under `results/parameter/`.
* Removed unused `s.plotBlend2Overall` setting and `helper_functions/plot_gamma.m`.
* Removed stale files: `helper_functions/norm_blend_voltage.m`, `helper_functions/plot_ocv_model_reconstruction.m`, `helper_functions/tum_colors.mat`, and shadowed `generate_si_ocp/1_generate_si_ocp_helper/load_blend.m`.
* Minor cleanups in `generate_si_ocp` (`path`/`pathSel` rename, `builtin('path')` use) and `import_ocv` (dead code removal, scalar checks).

## [2.0.0] - 2026-04-09

### Added
* Inhomogeneity offset for anode and cathode (`s.inhomAnodeOffset`, `s.inhomCathodeOffset`): allows a fraction of maximum inhomogeneity to be present already at SOC = 0 instead of starting from zero (allows no SOC dependence as well, which would be analogous to previous degradation mode analysis frameworks in literature).
* Isotonic regression for silicon OCP filtering in `generate_si_ocp` (replaces previous smoothing-based approach), producing strictly monotonic curves, while keeping maximum of information.
* 0C02 rate OCPs added to the input data pool alongside existing 0C03/0C04/0C05 rate curves.
* `import_ocv` now accepts `RPT`, `RPTs`, and `RPTNumber` columns for row lookup.
* Case-insensitive column matching in `import_ocv` (e.g. `'rpt'` and `'RPT'` both work).
* Case-insensitive name-value parsing in `import_ocv` (replaces `inputParser`).
* `fileNameFilter` setting for selecting specific MAT files in CU-folder mode.
* `.gitignore` rules for `.DS_Store` and generated result figures.

### Changed
* **Breaking:** renamed main entry point from `main_DMA` to `main_dma`; output struct from `Data` to `data`.
* **Breaking:** renamed `generate_si_OCP` to `generate_si_ocp`.
* **Breaking:** all file and folder names now use `snake_case`; all variables, struct fields, and function parameters use `lowerCamelCase`.
* **Breaking:** renamed `CheckUp` parameter to `checkUpIndex` in `import_ocv` and `get_full_cell_data`.
* Renamed internal solver data bundle from `myData` to `solverInput` across `dma_core`, `fit_ocv`, `fit_dva`, `fit_ica`, and `calculate_blend_curve`.
* Renamed `inputIsAging_data_table` to `inputIsAgingDataTable`.
* Renamed internal silicon-graphite references from `SiC` to `SiGr` for clarity.
* Consistent naming of graphite and silicon OCP input files.
* Simplified RMSE detection in `plot_dma` to use `rmseFullRange` only.
* Removed legacy `useBlendElectrodeModel` and `saveFig`/`savePathDMA` keys from `plot_dma`.
* Rewrote `README.md` to reflect current naming and usage.

### Fixed
* Fixed `varargin` passed as nested cell instead of expanded contents in `get_full_cell_data` CU-folder calls.
* Fixed missing `nameTableColumnOCV` and `inputIsAgingDataTable` arguments in CU-folder mode calls to `import_ocv`.
* Fixed non-monotonic regression in silicon OCP generation producing incorrect curves.
* Fixed UTF-8 encoding corruption (mojibake) in comments of `plot_dma` and `main_dma`.
* Removed dead `debugInhom` flag and unreachable code path in `calculate_inhomogeneity`.
* Removed tracked `.DS_Store` files.

## [1.0.0] - 2025-11-12

### Added
* Initial public release of Degradation Mode Analysis.
* Core workflow for mode identification.
* Command line interface and basic documentation.
